To address the issue of the edit text fields only snapping into view one at a time on smaller mobile displays, you can implement the following strategies:

1. **Use a `ScrollView`**: Since you are already using a `ScrollView`, ensure you have set the `android:fillViewport="true"` attribute. This enables the scroll view to fill the entire viewport, making all content visible when the keyboard comes up. From your provided layout context, you already have this in place ([SO-47148383]).

2. **Adjust the `windowSoftInputMode`**: You can set the `windowSoftInputMode` of your activity to `adjustPan` or `adjustResize` in the `AndroidManifest.xml` file. Using `adjustResize` is particularly beneficial as it allows the layout to resize when the keyboard appears, pushing other fields upwards and keeping them visible. Here’s how you would set it up:
   ```xml
   <activity
       android:name=".YourActivity"
       android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize">
   </activity>
   ```
   This can help ensure multiple input fields and buttons remain visible while the keyboard is up ([SO-45141273]).

3. **Focus Management**: If you are still facing issues of snapping, you can programmatically manage focus. Ensure the `EditText`s are able to receive focus by not blocking the descendants in your layout. If any parent layout has `android:descendantFocusability="blocksDescendants"`, remove it. This setting can prevent the `EditText` fields from receiving focus properly ([SO-50151141]).

4. **Using Event Listeners**: You might want to add a listener that detects when an `EditText` gains focus. Upon focusing, programmatically scroll to the view using:
   ```java
   yourScrollView.post(new Runnable() {
       @Override
       public void run() {
           yourScrollView.scrollTo(0, editText.getBottom());
       }
   });
   ```
   This will help in adjusting the view to make room for all input fields when focusing on any one of them ([SO-17738733]).

By integrating these changes into your layout and activity settings, you should achieve a more user-friendly interface where all input fields are visible when the keyboard is activated.

