Q: jQuery: Validating fields before submitting (multistep form)
A: <p>There's a very neat setting of jQuery validate that lets you ignore validation on hidden fields.  So you can handle the show/hide logic of your steps and for validation you could just do this:</p>

<p>As this suggests: <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2623514/jquery-validate-ignore-elements-with-style">ignore hidden</a></p>

<pre><code>$("form").validate({
   ignore: ":hidden"
});
</code></pre>

<p>If you need to check for validation on something besides the default form submit, you can use the <code>valid</code> method like this: <code>$("form").valid()</code>.</p>

<p>I noticed you don't have any validation classes on your form, so I'm assuming you're handling that somewhere else.  Just in case you're not, you can tell jQuery validate your rules through css classes like this: <code>&lt;input type="text" class="required digits"/&gt;</code></p>

<p>See more here: <a href="http://bassistance.de/2008/01/30/jquery-validation-plugin-overview/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">http://bassistance.de/2008/01/30/jquery-validation-plugin-overview/</a></p>

